Can't imagine that {be} is grammatical here like it's in e.g. {pa djine be lo solji/lo rijno/lo fagri etc.}
{ro ko'a} doesn't seem bad
{facki ko'a} will not work out the sense like {facki zi'o ko'a} might do; better: {tolcri ko'a}
{gi'e *va'o* le nu manku} seems to be less natlang idiomatic than {ne'i/nenri le manku} or even {mankyne'i ralte ko'a}

